{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/23074-suggestions-for-a-creature-ability-please","id":23074,"title":"Suggestions for a creature ability please","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-04T05:30:08-08:00","id":23074,"title":"Suggestions for a creature ability please","content":"hi, im writing a story featuring a spirit-like creature with the powers relating to cold, sort of a &quot;frost wraith&quot; or something. basically, what im stuck on is how to handle its basic attack where it would inflict severe hypothermia/frostbite in a matter of moments. Ive read and reread the rules in nWoD rulebbok relating to cold and it doesnt seem to fit whats in my mind. What i would like to do is have the PCs make a 'save' if you will against the creature's attack (in which case Stamina should do the trick imo) just so they have a sense of resisting the things onslaught. What makes sense to me to do, and i would really appreciate suggestions here most, is make the 'cold attack' an attribute + skill/merit roll like any other attack, just to make things easier on myself. If anyone has any ideas or suggestions on this, or has cooked up a similar creature power, i'd very much like to hear them. also, i am rather new to nWoD (though i have played several other RPGs) and am still somewhat a noob on the rules, so if i apologize if this comes off as a boneheaded question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T06:09:34-08:00","id":23094,"title":"","content":"Not boneheaded at all.<br /> <br /> For the frostbite, here's what I can remember<br /> In Changeling there's a sort of frost aura someone can surround themselves with, so that up to 20 feet out anyone approaching has a -1 to dice rolls because it's so cold (and another -1 for every five consecutive rounds they stay in the area).<br /> And the Extreme Cold tilt in God Machine Chronicle, which is similar, in that there's a -1 penalty to all rolls, increasing every hour until they hit -5, when they start taking lethal damage from the cold. In addition, bashing damage doesn't heal as long as you're in the extreme cold area (which could be in your case represented by the wraith's frostbite affect, perhaps only curable by a blessing from a priest or warming yourself in a fire started by a child, or something).<br /> Lastly I suppose you could do an invert of the Dread Power Balefire. So that if something actually gets close enough to touch the wraith they take some lethal damage from the cold.<br /> <br /> Some mix of those might be appropriate, weaker or more powerful as you need it.<br /> <br /> As for rolls, yeah, Stamina seems like a nice defense, perhaps Stamina/Survival, I want to say Stamina/Athletics but can't help but think being fit might be detrimental to the situation. As for its attack, maybe Presence + Frostbite, you could just give the inherent power of the wraith a few dots (maybe 'weak' frost wraiths get one dot, while the supreme ancient master frost wraith gets 5). Presence if it's an Aura, Strength if it's a melee-like attack, Dex if it's a beam or aimed thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-04-2013, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T13:40:24-08:00","id":23294,"title":"","content":"thanks mate. that helps immensely <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> i think that since what i have in mind is something incorporeal and unbeatable directly i'll use your suggestion for Presence for all of it's attacks; aura/touch/breath/ect, if only to make it most dangerous and my life easier ;P<br /> <br /> if it helps you to help me, the wraith i have in mind is to be quite powerful, in fact even bordering on over powered for my (beginning) players. basically its unkillable, but can be 'dispelled' by destroying the object to which its bound. the creature, i think, would have 3 attacks, an aura, a 'breath' and a touch each tied to Presence as it really cant 'breathe' or 'touch' its victim. though i do admit i cut my roleplaying teeth on DnD where incorporeal use charisma for most applications, so im not sure if that would apply to nWoD? please correct me if my interpretation is mistaken on this.<br /> <br /> also the Stamina + Survival is an excellent idea. i hadn't thought of the skill but i agree with your take on Athletics being slightly unfit, since it seems to me that being able to run or climb doesn't make one better at resisting the cold. but since im not a 'rules lawyer' i would absolutely welcome a differing opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T14:03:29-08:00","id":23301,"title":"","content":"Just spitballing here; although the idea of a resistance roll is fine, why not have something like this: (also I'm not exactly up with all the rules so please excuse any gross errors!)<br /> <br /> <b>Frostburn <span style=\"font-family:arial\">(</span></b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Make an attack roll as normal (Melee, ranged, or Aura as appropriate). If it hits, in addition to normal damage mark Bashing damage in a number of boxes equal to the level of this Power, putting a snowflake symbol ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) under those extra boxes. As long as a character has any wound penalties and also has boxes marked with a snowflake that character has -1 to all dice pools. If a character falls unconscious while it has wound boxes marked with a snowflake, they suffer from the condition <b>Hypothermia.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Hypothermia (Condition)</b><br /> The character is suffering from Hypothermia and is in grave danger of dying.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> In addition to extra wounds inflicted while unconscious, one bashing damage is converted to lethal each minute the character suffers from this condition.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> An Int + Medicine roll, penalised by the number of wound boxes marked with a snowflake symbol<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> This makes Frostburn <i><b>very</b></i> deadly at higher levels; beware!!</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":568,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","user":"Viperion","date":".  Changed name from Frostbite to Frostburn b/c it sounds cooler 12-04-2013, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T15:51:32-08:00","id":23361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Viperion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/23074-suggestions-for-a-creature-ability-please?p=23301#post23301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just spitballing here; although the idea of a resistance roll is fine, why not have something like this: (also I'm not exactly up with all the rules so please excuse any gross errors!)<br /> <br /> <b>Frostburn <span style=\"font-family:arial\">(</span></b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Make an attack roll as normal (Melee, ranged, or Aura as appropriate). If it hits, in addition to normal damage mark Bashing damage in a number of boxes equal to the level of this Power, putting a snowflake symbol ( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) under those extra boxes. As long as a character has any wound penalties and also has boxes marked with a snowflake that character has -1 to all dice pools. If a character falls unconscious while it has wound boxes marked with a snowflake, they suffer from the condition <b>Hypothermia.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Hypothermia (Condition)</b><br /> The character is suffering from Hypothermia and is in grave danger of dying.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> In addition to extra wounds inflicted while unconscious, one bashing damage is converted to lethal each minute the character suffers from this condition.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> An Int + Medicine roll, penalised by the number of wound boxes marked with a snowflake symbol<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> This makes Frostburn <i><b>very</b></i> deadly at higher levels; beware!!</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>wow! thats so close to what i was thinking its scary... but in a good way :P thank you so much! only question i have now is for the Frostburn... what attribute should i use for the attack roll? would it be Presence or something different entirely? other than that i think it'll work for my critter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T16:21:02-08:00","id":23377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>munkieboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/23074-suggestions-for-a-creature-ability-please?p=23361#post23361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wow! thats so close to what i was thinking its scary... but in a good way :P thank you so much! only question i have now is for the Frostburn... what attribute should i use for the attack roll? would it be Presence or something different entirely? other than that i think it'll work for my critter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cool<br /> <br /> It depends on the attack and the type of critter; the off the cuff answer is &quot;Whatever you think is appropriate&quot; but if your beastie has a full stat block I'd go with Dex + Athletics for the ranged attack, Dex + Brawl for the melee &quot;Chill Touch&quot; and not sure what I'd do with an Aura attack; that's beyond my understanding of the system :P<br /> <br /> However I'd be tempted to use them as Sprits as per the GMC, and only have Power, Finesse and Resistance traits. In that case all three attacks could use Power + Finesse vs the defending characters Defence.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not an expert and these may be way off as suggestions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T19:00:43-08:00","id":23449,"title":"","content":"d'oh! forgot the spirit attributes lol. that seems to work. thanks again, you've sundered my writing block <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/993-munkieboi","name":"munkieboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar993_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}